<BaseLayout title="Fuses and electrical units">
  <h1>Fuses and electrical units</h1>
  <p>Volvo identifies three main central electrical-unit locations for the left-hand-drive 2021 S60: engine compartment, under the glove compartment, and cargo area. The vehicle's own fuse chart is the authority for individual fuse numbers and amperages.</p>

  <figure class="reference-photo reference-diagram">
    <a class="reference-photo-link" href="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      <img src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine compartment overview showing the central electrical unit location" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </a>
    <figcaption>Volvo 2021 S60 engine-compartment overview. Callout 4 identifies the central electrical unit; the illustration does not show individual fuse assignments or the other fuse-box locations.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <ReferencePhoto src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/imgd95efd27ae92616bc0a801521f2a3c23_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" variant="reference-diagram" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine-compartment fuse panel with numbered fuse positions" caption="Volvo 2021 S60 engine-compartment fuse layout. Use the diagram on the vehicle's fuse-box cover to verify the installed configuration." credit="Volvo Cars" source="https://www.volvocars.com/en-ca/support/car/s60/2021/article/1f2a2f75c7fab5e2c0a81f6f0da34d7b/f40a54afc7fb5bf5c0a81f6f74c5b3b7/ca7567a57067c65dc0a8015174bfa78b/" license="Volvo Cars support illustration" />

  <h2>Locations</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Engine compartment:</strong> central electrical unit in the engine bay.</li>
    <li><strong>Under the glove compartment:</strong> central electrical unit protecting several cabin electrical functions.</li>
    <li><strong>Cargo area:</strong> central electrical unit for rear and other vehicle functions.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note"><strong>Left-hand-drive / right-hand-drive:</strong> Volvo notes that the under-glovebox unit changes sides on right-hand-drive vehicles. This site is primarily organized around North American, left-hand-drive examples.</p>

  <h2>Safe fuse inspection</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Identify the failed function and consult the correct fuse chart for this exact car.</li>
    <li>Switch off the vehicle and follow Volvo's instructions before accessing the fuse.</li>
    <li>Remove the specified fuse using the proper fuse tool and inspect its element.</li>
    <li>If blown, replace it only with the same type and amperage.</li>
    <li>If the new fuse fails, do not fit another. The circuit may have a short or component fault.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Critical warnings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Never use a higher-rated fuse, wire, foil, or another object in place of a fuse.</li>
    <li>Do not replace fuses for circuits not described in the owner's information without qualified service guidance.</li>
    <li>Do not assume fuse positions are identical across model years, markets, or equipment levels.</li>
  </ul>

